exercises.text:
10m, .22 Rimfire Pistol Rapid Fire Exercise 
 FIREARMS PERMITTED:  Only Semi-Automatic Pistols in .22S, .22LR & .22 Mag Calibres (al types of sight configurations allowed)
 SHOOTING DISTANCE:   The shooting distance measured from the target to the edge of the firing line closest to the shooter is 10 meters.
 COURSE OF FIRE:   10 shots at 10m in 30 seconds shot on the correct exercise specific target in your own time, and scored out of 100 points.
1.   Load 10 rounds in magazine;
2.   De-cock pistol on empty chamber with hammer down – magazine in pistol;
3.   On start signal, cock pistol and fire string of 10 shots at prescribed target @ 10 metres;
4.   Participants may use pre-loaded second magazine if first magazine does not take 10 rounds;
 Note:   Time for exercise to be completed is 30 Seconds.  Timing starts when time keeper gives the command Start (Fire) and ends when the last shot has been fired.
 FIRING POSITION:   Standing position, Rimfire Pistol held in one or both hands, with all portions of the shooter`s clothing, body and firearm clear of artificial support

